The template accepts `std::array` with `size > 0`. For a vector, it will check in debug but in release calling the function on an empty vector results in undefined behaviour.

Example usage:
```c++
static constexpr auto wooshingNoiseIds = std::array<audio::SoundId, 4> {
    audio::SoundId::G_Woosh_01,
    audio::SoundId::G_Woosh_02,
    audio::SoundId::G_Woosh_03,
    audio::SoundId::G_Woosh_04,
};
const auto wooshNoiseId = static_cast<entt::id_type>(Locator::rng::value().Choose(wooshingNoiseIds));
```

```c++
std::vector<audio::SoundId> wooshingNoiseIds;
wooshingNoiseIds.push_back(audio::SoundId::G_Woosh_01);
wooshingNoiseIds.push_back(audio::SoundId::G_Woosh_02);
wooshingNoiseIds.push_back(audio::SoundId::G_Woosh_03);
wooshingNoiseIds.push_back(audio::SoundId::G_Woosh_04);
const auto wooshNoiseId = static_cast<entt::id_type>(Locator::rng::value().Choose(wooshingNoiseIds));
```

